Crysknives are perfectly viable, yes.  My wife's atheist is currently
wielding a +7 crysknife and doing fairly well.  But, there's no reason to
limit as many games as this would limit to that -- sure, on very rare
occasions or due to special conducts, a crysknife might be your best
weapon.  But it shouldn't be forced on you on a regular basis.  I already
make the best of what I get on a regular basis (I was wearing crystal
plate mail for a while recently), and often impose extra conducts to force
myself to do even more.  I'd rather not have the game impose that conduct
on me because I happen to be somewhat unlucky with altars...

I think nyra explained it well -- it's fixing a hole that just isn't
there.  It's enforcing a low-artifact conduct that many of us would rather
self-impose, or impose via atheism, or whatever.  Those who don't descend,
and just stick around at altars saccing for hours on end, do so because
they want to -- if you're sick of it, don't do it.  Play artifactless, or
play atheist, or play a speed game, or whatever.

> You think? Most people, from what I see, sacrifice for these reasons:
