e) to get spellbooks
f) to get golden glows
g) to get AC
h) to get intrinsics
i) to get rid of trolls

In terms of how important they are to my games, I'd rank them
g-e-a-h-f-b-i-c-d (granted, e wouldn't be so important if I didn't play
primarily casters...)

Also, (a) need not be THE artifact, just one I find useful -- which
includes any lawful artifact except Demonbane, plus Magicbane, Mojo,
Vorpy, Stormy, Fire or Frost.  The new patch would add demonbane,
giantslayer, and maybe Dragonbane to my list of good ascension
artifacts... and trollsbane, ogremasher, and grimtooth to my list of
useful mid-game artifacts.

What the original patch does is removes choice (a) from consideration,
meaning there is no longer a real choice between "keep saccing without
praying" and "pray every time you get reconciliation".

I think people would compensate for not getting a decent artifact by
sticking around for more spellbooks / golden glows / AC.  So I don't think
this at all will encourage people to keep moving down through the
dungeon... rather, it'll just reduce their options, and make them more
likely to stick around at an altar for a lot LONGER to try to buff up
their character enough to feel safe descending.

Reducing options is sometimes a Good Thing (TM) -- it's good to force
players to work with what they have sometimes -- but I think people, for
the most part, use conducts to accomplish this already.  And in this case,
reducing the average game to maybe 3-4 artifacts and a crysknife is, IMO,
the same order of difficulty as a reasonable conduct like Genoless or
polyselfless.  It's excessive, and doesn't really match up well with the
rest of the stated goals of the patch.  And that is a Bad Thing (TM)

Making the limitation come in once there are a few artifacts in the game
would be fairly reasonable -- if you really can't get an artifact you're
happy with by the fifth or sixth, you need to be less picky.  But if you
don't get an artifact you're happy with by the first or second, you're
probably pretty normal.



